WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:01.786
- God and just when you think it stops

00:00:01.786 --> 00:00:03.786
it just starts up again.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.692
Yeah, I'm ready for it to be done.

00:00:06.692 --> 00:00:09.192
(light music)

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:15.079
- Today we're doing a
simulation of hearing voices.

00:00:15.079 --> 00:00:17.426
- I have never done
anything like this before.

00:00:17.426 --> 00:00:21.552
- I'm doing the simulation
today for my brother.

00:00:21.552 --> 00:00:24.815
He was diagnosed with
schizophrenia recently.

00:00:24.815 --> 00:00:26.973
- I have a few family members

00:00:26.973 --> 00:00:28.576
who have delit with schizophrenia.

00:00:28.576 --> 00:00:30.807
I'd like to understand how big the gulf

00:00:30.807 --> 00:00:34.431
between the way I experience
the world and the way

00:00:34.431 --> 00:00:36.587
someone with schizophrenia
would experience the world.

00:00:36.587 --> 00:00:38.757
- My nae is Autumn and I am schizophrenic.

00:00:38.757 --> 00:00:41.674
I was diagnosed with
schizophrenia in 2015.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.452
I can particularly identify

00:00:43.452 --> 00:00:45.244
two different voices from my past.

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:49.679
One is a kind of raspy,
masculine, deep, dark voice

00:00:49.679 --> 00:00:52.369
that usually says my name multiple times

00:00:52.369 --> 00:00:55.870
and another voice usually tells
me to go different places.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:58.892
I've heard up to five
different voices at one time

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:01.527
all talking about different subjects

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:02.846
and crowding my head in chaos.

00:01:02.846 --> 00:01:05.638
It is already hard enough
for people with schizophrenia

00:01:05.638 --> 00:01:07.357
to deal with it every single day.

00:01:07.357 --> 00:01:08.967
Try to understand our situation

00:01:08.967 --> 00:01:10.942
and how it might be
from our point of view.

00:01:10.942 --> 00:01:14.612
- I guess I'm expecting
a new understanding.

00:01:14.612 --> 00:01:16.553
- I'm feeling a little nervous
about this, I gotta say.

00:01:16.553 --> 00:01:19.706
I hope it provides a
different perspective.

00:01:19.706 --> 00:01:22.845
- [Recording] I said you stop it now.

00:01:22.845 --> 00:01:25.452
Look at it, eyes are everywhere.

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:28.702
Filthy, filthy filthy, the smell of it.

00:01:29.765 --> 00:01:32.795
No good, that's right, absolutely.

00:01:32.795 --> 00:01:36.935
- I'm gonna start the auditory
hallucination simulator

00:01:36.935 --> 00:01:39.635
and then just try to do
some basic household chores.

00:01:39.635 --> 00:01:43.767
I just started it and I
gotta say it's really creepy.

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:45.851
I was gonna try to put away some dishes

00:01:45.851 --> 00:01:47.545
but I can't really focus.

00:01:47.545 --> 00:01:51.417
- There's a lot of
whisper, there's a lot of

00:01:51.417 --> 00:01:53.709
oh my gosh, this is really creepy.

00:01:53.709 --> 00:01:56.450
- So I'm like 10 minutes in right now

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:59.472
and it's seriously like terrifying

00:01:59.472 --> 00:02:03.639
but I only take solace in
the sorry, I can't think.

00:02:05.117 --> 00:02:07.962
I know it's a simulation
and I know I could

00:02:07.962 --> 00:02:10.029
take the headphones off at any time

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:12.334
but I'm determined to keep them on,

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:13.970
at the same time very freaked out.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.345
That's hard to articulate.

00:02:15.345 --> 00:02:19.151
- Now I really feel like
I can't get sentences out.

00:02:19.151 --> 00:02:22.134
One of them just told me I was disgusting.

00:02:22.134 --> 00:02:23.846
- I tried going for a walk
to kind of pass the time.

00:02:23.846 --> 00:02:26.865
I gotta say being
outside in an environment

00:02:26.865 --> 00:02:30.552
that isn't where I live but
I can't really control fully

00:02:30.552 --> 00:02:32.324
is even more terrifying.

00:02:32.324 --> 00:02:34.228
- As I'm seeing all of this I'm listening

00:02:34.228 --> 00:02:35.860
through all of this and I'm
kind of just experiencing

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.757
how hard it is to put sentences together,

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:41.622
how hard it is to talk or
explain or do anything.

00:02:41.622 --> 00:02:45.771
- I know it's a simulation
but some of the cruelty

00:02:45.771 --> 00:02:48.421
really resonates, really hits home.

00:02:48.421 --> 00:02:51.248
Okay, so I'm just lying in bed now.

00:02:51.248 --> 00:02:54.005
It's the only thing that feels comfortable

00:02:54.005 --> 00:02:57.759
is just lying in total
darkness, I'm ready to be done.

00:02:57.759 --> 00:02:59.977
I finished the auditory
hallucination simulator

00:02:59.977 --> 00:03:01.894
about five minutes ago.

00:03:03.109 --> 00:03:04.789
I feel like I still hear it.

00:03:04.789 --> 00:03:08.539
- I just did a short
meditation here at home.

00:03:09.815 --> 00:03:13.065
I would not have been able to do that

00:03:13.065 --> 00:03:15.122
with the audio on at all.

00:03:15.122 --> 00:03:19.497
It takes a lot to listen
through the voices.

00:03:19.497 --> 00:03:21.126
- So it's the next day.

00:03:21.126 --> 00:03:25.580
Some of the more cruel
phrases like you eat shit

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:29.592
or you stink, you hear
it over and over and over

00:03:29.592 --> 00:03:33.759
and over and over again and it
starts to really affect you.

00:03:34.793 --> 00:03:36.192
It wore me out.

00:03:36.192 --> 00:03:37.640
- I do feel closer to my brother now.

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:40.797
This was a great eye opening experience.

00:03:40.797 --> 00:03:43.837
- I still would not willingly go through

00:03:43.837 --> 00:03:45.147
something like that again.

00:03:45.147 --> 00:03:48.587
It's allowed me to access
that empathy for them.

00:03:48.587 --> 00:03:50.440
- It's our job to learn more.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:51.999
- If I could say anything to people

00:03:51.999 --> 00:03:53.897
who do not have
schizophrenia, I would just

00:03:53.897 --> 00:03:56.761
like to tell them to not
judge others so harshly.

00:03:56.761 --> 00:03:58.836
We are mostly just misunderstood.

00:03:58.836 --> 00:04:01.994
We are able to make a living,
we are able to raise families,

00:04:01.994 --> 00:04:03.771
and I hope that one day
everyone in the world

00:04:03.771 --> 00:04:05.022
is able to see that.

00:04:05.022 --> 00:04:08.022
(light piano music)

